.claude/
.playwright-mcp/
dist/
node_modules/
outputs/
source-photos/

# Raw project walkthrough footage — hundreds of MB each, and public/ ships
# to Vercel. Ad cuts live in marketing/meta-ads/renders/ instead.
public/images/*.mp4
public/images/*.mov
__pycache__/
# Scratch only. ai-source/ is deliberately NOT ignored: those clips cost
# credits and cannot be regenerated identically - the model is stochastic,
# so a re-roll gives different motion and may reintroduce artefacts we
# already checked out. Losing them means F2, F3 and Z2 cannot be rebuilt.
marketing/meta-ads/_*
marketing/meta-ads/upload-to-meta/

# Raw client media staging - originals live in Drive, never in the repo
Pending/

# two-pass x264 stats files - scratch, regenerated every encode
marketing/meta-ads/renders/_*.log
marketing/meta-ads/renders/_*.mbtree

# Silent masters. add_music() muxes the track with `-c:v copy`, so the video
# bitstream in `--reels-video.mp4` is byte-identical to its `-music` twin -
# checked across all 30 pairs, no exceptions. Tracking both stored every cut
# twice to carry a ~400 KB AAC stream, ~349 MB in total.
#
# Untracking does NOT keep them on disk: checking out or merging this commit
# deletes them from the working tree, ignore rules and all. That is fine - a
# silent master is recovered from its `-music` twin losslessly in about a
# second, because the video stream is a straight copy either way:
#
#     ffmpeg -i <cut>--reels-video-music.mp4 -c:v copy -an <cut>--reels-video.mp4
#
# The recovered file is not byte-identical to the one git held - ffmpeg
# rewrites the container, so muxer tags and faststart layout differ - but the
# H.264 stream inside is bit-for-bit the same, checked on all 34. The picture
# is exact; only the wrapper is new. Worth having locally when swapping a track
# (MUSIC.md shows that happens), since re-muxing beats a `-crf 19` rebuild -
# but it is derived, not a master, so git should not carry it.
marketing/meta-ads/renders/*--reels-video.mp4
marketing/meta-ads/renders/*--feed-video.mp4

# Meta API token - never commit this
marketing/meta-ads/.token

# Story cards ARE committed - about 10 MB for 30, and Eric posts from this
# folder by hand. Regenerable from build_stories.py, but a deliverable he
# uses should not live only on one machine.

# Motion clips rendered from stills - regenerated by build_stills.py
marketing/meta-ads/_stills/

# End-card animation intermediates - regenerated by build_progress.py
marketing/meta-ads/renders/*--endcard.mp4
